 ## Subtopics
 
 ### Closest Hit Texture Initialization
-A fragment shader pass that initializes the closest hit texture to a value indicating no hit (e.g., `vec4(-1)`). This is used to reset the accumulation buffer when the scene changes or at the start of rendering [S3, unofficial].
+A fragment shader pass that initializes the closest hit texture to a value indicating no hit (e.g., `vec4(-1)`). [S3, unofficial] This is used to reset the accumulation buffer when the scene changes or at the start of rendering [S3, unofficial].
 
 ### Accumulation Integration
-A rendering pass that blends an accumulated buffer with a new frame using a mixing factor. It selects the closest depth/position between the current frame's result and the accumulated history to maintain a stable isosurface view. If both have valid depth (`w > 0`), it selects the one with smaller `w` (closer to camera) [S5, unofficial].
