 ### Running Average Integration
-A technique to compute a running average of frames using the inverse frame number. The accumulator is updated as `acc + (frame - acc) * uInvFrameNumber`, where `uInvFrameNumber` is the inverse of the current frame number [S5, unofficial].
+A technique to compute a running average of frames using the inverse frame number. [S5, unofficial] The accumulator is updated as `acc + (frame - acc) * uInvFrameNumber`, where `uInvFrameNumber` is the inverse of the current frame number [S5, unofficial].
 
 ### Temporal Layer Averaging
-A fragment shader pass that averages color values across multiple layers of a 2D texture array. It loops through all layers, sums the values, and divides by the number of layers. This is used for temporal accumulation or history blending in rendering pipelines [S1, unofficial].
